# Local build args. `.env.example` is the TEMPLATE and stays tracked; the file it
# is copied to does not. Since the status wiring landed, that copy holds an
# `ik_…` and a `wk_…` — both public once a bundle ships, but still deployment
# configuration, which CLAUDE.md keeps in Coolify rather than in the repo. A
# committed key is also one that rotation silently leaves behind.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

